# R5 Reduction Test: Unit-typed enum constructors become nullary

Tests that enum constructors carrying Unit are emitted as nullary constructors
in Lean4, simplifying both declarations and usage sites.

Before R5 reduction:
```
inductive Color : Type where
 | Red : Unit -> Color
 | Blue : Unit -> Color
 | Custom : Int -> Color

-- construction:  (Color.Red ())
-- pattern match: | Color.Red x => ...
-- equality test: decide (c = (Color.Red ()))
```

After R5 reduction:
```
inductive Color : Type where
 | Red : Color
 | Blue : Color
 | Custom : Int -> Color

-- construction:  Color.Red
-- pattern match: | Color.Red => ...
-- equality test: decide (c = Color.Red)
```

Note: runtime library enums like Optional are NOT changed:
  `(Optional.Absent ())` and `| Optional.Absent _ =>` remain as-is.

```catala
declaration enumeration Color:
  -- Red
  -- Blue
  -- Custom content integer

declaration scope PaintMixer:
  input color content Color
  output color_code content integer
  output is_custom content boolean

scope PaintMixer:
  definition color_code equals match color with pattern
    -- Red : 1
    -- Blue : 2
    -- Custom content x : x

  definition is_custom equals match color with pattern
    -- Red : false
    -- Blue : false
    -- Custom content x : true
```
